# Two environments mixed by IEM with a reaction too fast for A and B to coexist.
# Every environment relaxes to the mean mixture fraction, 0.3, at omega = Cphi/2
# epsilon/k = 0.25 1/s: xi_i(t) = 0.3 + (xi_i(0) - 0.3) exp(-omega t), from zero
# and from one, with weights 0.7 and 0.3. What A and B are made of is linear in
# the mixture fraction, so an environment holds the product of the complete
# reaction of the two streams mixed at its mixture fraction, 0.2 min(xi_i, 1 -
# xi_i), and the mean is the sum over the two.
# t [s]   xi_0   xi_1   mean Y_P   mean Y_A   mean Y_B
